{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>ואהי שובר</b> — from <b>ויסבר</b> 'to make hated.' And from the language of our Rabbis, may their memory be blessed: סברא. And the sense is: I was thinking and examining the walls." "<b>המפורצים</b> — in the manner of <b>מזה בידך מלכם תדכאו עמי</b>. But the men of the Masorah punctuated it with a short [form] for brevity, and the open mem hints at walls that are open and breached — this is the way of derash, and the first way is correct in my eyes."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:15.100922270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}